Done. The temporary test file is removed; only `src/store.rs` is modified.

## What changed

Added `pub fn rename` to `rust/src/store.rs:17-58`. It:
1. Reads `{old_id}.note` and parses it with the same `splitn(4, "\n---\n")` as `load_all`.
2. Errors if the file is malformed (`parts.len() != 4`) or the stored first field doesn't match `old_id`.
3. Rebuilds the note with the new id/title while keeping the pinned flag (`parts[2]`) and body (`parts[3]`) intact — so tags are recomputed by `load_all` from the unchanged body.
4. Writes `{new_id}.note` **first**, then deletes `{old_id}.note` only if `new_id != old_id` — so a failed write never destroys the note.

## Verified
- `cargo build` and `cargo test` (existing `basic.rs`) pass.
- A temporary test suite (now removed) confirmed end-to-end: after `rename`, `load_all(dir)` returns exactly one note with the new id + title, body/tags/pinned preserved, old file gone, new file present; `new_id == old_id` overwrites in place; missing old id and corrupt content both error without removing the old file.

The public API matches the requested signature exactly:
```rust
pub fn rename(dir: &Path, old_id: &str, new_id: &str, new_title: &str) -> std::io::Result<()>
```


